From 73200aae25f27a9a5417b0f5d52faa925f6764dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 22:29:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 098/115] clk: qcom: mmcc-msm8998: keep the MMSS config NoC AHB
 clock on

Enabling any MMSS branch while mnoc_ahb_clk is gated writes the enable
bit and then times out waiting for the halt bit to clear, because the
CBCR being polled is itself behind the MMSS config NoC. The consumer
gets -EBUSY.

On a Pixel 2 XL this makes the camera depend on probe order. The CCI
I2C controller probes before the display, finds nothing has voted for
the NoC yet, and dies:

	camss_ahb_clk status stuck at 'off'
	WARNING: drivers/clk/qcom/clk-branch.c:88 clk_branch_toggle
	Failed to enable clk 'camss_ahb': -16
	i2c-qcom-cci ca0c000.cci: probe with driver i2c-qcom-cci
		failed with error -16

No CCI means no camera I2C bus, so neither sensor is discovered and
the media graph comes up with no sources. Binding the same driver by
hand after the display controller has taken its own mnoc_ahb_clk
reference succeeds immediately and both sensors appear, which is what
identified the clock.

gcc_mmss_noc_cfg_ahb_clk is already marked critical for the same
reason one level up; this is the MMSS-internal half of the same path.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
index 7f1d0f0da0bc..1cc49970299d 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
@@ -2451,7 +2451,15 @@ static struct clk_branch mnoc_ahb_clk = {
 			.parent_hws = (const struct clk_hw *[]){ &ahb_clk_src.clkr.hw },
 			.num_parents = 1,
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
-			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+			/*
+			 * The MMSS config NoC carries every register access
+			 * inside MMSS, including the CBCRs of this controller's
+			 * own branches. With it gated a branch enable writes
+			 * the enable bit and then times out waiting for the
+			 * halt bit, so the consumer sees -EBUSY. Same reason
+			 * gcc_mmss_noc_cfg_ahb_clk is critical one level up.
+			 */
+			.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 		},
 	},
 };
